// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Lantern Row Games LLC: two owners (60/40), taxed as an S-corp, sells board games and puzzles online and does
// some consulting. Austin, Texas. Payroll: the officer (an owner) and three employees. Sales tax collected in Texas and Washington. 2025-11-01 .. 2026-03-31.
//
// Written against docs/v5/PROPOSAL.md §6 (`->` gives, `<-` takes, `@` exchanges, legs lead with arrows, positions
// under agents, a debt is a promise, direction decides income or spending, the counterparty is optional) and the
// typed associations of ASSOCIATIONS.md. Not runnable: no toolchain reads it.
//
//   ✗ cannot say     ✎ says it badly     ? unclear     ⇄ what sync would need     ▸ derived, never typed
//
// Each mark carries an id (sb-c13: small business, c = cannot say, 13) and the change in REPORT.md that closes it:
// [A1]..[A12] are this lane's twelve; [K5] says PROPOSAL §5 already closes it; [open] says nothing here does.
// The index at the end of the file lists every id once.
//
// About the numbers. This is the last five months of a book that began in 2023: journal/2025/01..10.ax are not shown.
// Every figure was produced by a script that replayed each event through an internal double-entry check (a tool for
// the author, never part of the language). Cash, FIFO cost, payroll, FICA, FUTA and SUTA bases, sales tax, Stripe
// fees, interest on the line and the EUR conversion are exact; net assets moved by exactly income less distributions.
// Payroll uses the 2026 brackets of crates/systems/src/us.ax as an approximation of IRS Pub 15-T; rates marked verify
// are illustrative. Exchange rates are illustrative.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

base USD
use us
use us/tx                  // sales tax, no income tax, SUTA through the Texas Workforce Commission (twc)
use us/wa                  // sales tax by destination; B&O tax is left out of this book
use us/payroll             // kind employment: withholding, FICA both halves, FUTA, SUTA, the plan match  [A3]
use us/s-corp              // kind s-corp: what the business counts, its owners count in their shares   [A4]

// ── people ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/// Dana Okafor, 60%, the officer. She is `me` in this book.
entity dana : person
  born    1984-08-17
  filing  single
  lives   us/tx

/// Theo Lindqvist, 40%. A buyer and event person, part time; he is paid by distribution and his own note.
entity theo : person
  born    1982-03-02
  filing  single
  lives   us/tx

entity marisol, kenji, jonah : person         // employees. Not owners: nobody's money here is theirs
  filing  single
  lives   us/tx

// ── the company ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/// Lantern Row Games LLC. The positions are written under their owner: the nesting fills `owner`, the path
/// (`chase/operating`) fills `with`. Both are slots of the position's kind, and the kind says what may fill them. [A2]
entity lantern-row : s-corp
  owners  dana 60%, theo 40%                  // a weighted many-slot: shares by day, so selling 10% on 09-01 splits the K-1 at that day  [A4]
  books   accrual
  lives   us/tx
  lives   us/wa from 2025-04-01               // ✎ sb-b01 [A12] `lives` is a domicile for a person; for a company this is nexus, which its own tallies cross

  chase/operating   : deposit
  stripe/balance    : processor-balance       // what Stripe owes the company until it pays out
    pays out weekly on tuesday all into operating
  wise/eur          : deposit holds EUR
  wise/usd          : deposit
  amex/card         : credit-card
    in full monthly on 25 from operating      // a card is a promise too: the forecast sees the bill
  bluebonnet/line   : credit-line 40_000 USD  // ✗ sb-c04 [A7] a revolving line: draws and repayments at will, interest on the daily balance,
    rate prime + 2.5%                         //   a floating rate. v5's `loan` is the annuity; ACTUS has UMP and IPAC for this
    pays interest monthly on 5 for last month from operating
  theo/note         : loan 15_000.00 USD on 2024-03-01 at 6%     // a debt is a position with a promise (§6.2): theo is `with`, by the path
    interest monthly on 28 from operating     // ✗ sb-c05 [A8] interest only, the principal in one payment (ACTUS PAM): v5's `loan` is the annuity
  warehouse         : stock-room              // custody by the company itself, as cash in hand is
  label-printer     : equipment               // bought 2025-10-12 for 6_800 USD; see the opening

  401k-plan                                   // a thing of kind 401k-plan, named by its kind: sponsor = lantern-row by the nesting
    custodian guideline                       // the recordkeeper: a slot of kind 401k-plan, filled by role word
    match 100% to 3%, 50% to 5%               // ✎ sb-b07 [A1] a tiered match is a typed value of the plan, not an expression written in every `also`

// ── who the company deals with ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

entity chase, bluebonnet : bank
entity amex : card-issuer
entity stripe : processor
entity wise : money-transfer
entity guideline : recordkeeper
entity irs, tx-comptroller, wa-dor, twc : tax-authority
entity pecan-st : landlord                    // the warehouse
entity brightwood-dist, boxcraft : vendor     // games and puzzles; the club's boxes
entity oakcraft : vendor                      // ? sb-u08 [A12] it is a vendor now and a client in February: kinds here are roles, and a thing has one kind
entity ups-freight, pirate-ship, uline : vendor
entity austin-energy : utility
entity spectrum : isp
entity hartford : insurer
entity meta-ads, mailchimp : advertiser
entity home-depot, staples, costco, eventbrite : merchant
entity austin-food-bank #charity
entity priya-nair : contractor                // the bookkeeper: 1099-NEC
  w9 true
entity lumi-studio : contractor               // box artwork, once
  w9 true
entity barton-dental, east-side-brewing, southside-library : client
entity cafe-cluiche : client                  // Dublin; pays in EUR
entity customers : market                     // every shopper, as one party: v5 lets a flow omit its counterparty, but a document header reads better with one

// ── what is sold ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/// Goods bought to be sold again. A sale is revenue and a cost, never a capital gain. [A9]
kind merchandise : stock-in-trade
  select fifo                                 // average cost would be `prorata`: relief in exact shares of every parcel
  sells  sales                                // ✎ sb-b03 [A9] the purpose of selling a commodity is a property of its kind; v4's `pays` is for issuers
commodity ORCHARD    : merchandise            // a strategy game
commodity LANTERN    : merchandise            // a card game
commodity ALPINE_1K  : merchandise            // a 1,000-piece puzzle
commodity DICE_OAK   : merchandise            // hand-turned dice
commodity TILEWRIGHT : merchandise            // the heavy strategy game
commodity CLUB_BOX   : merchandise            // one box of the Game Night Club

// ── employment, a plan, a lease, a note: contracts are typed and fill slots ──────────────────────────

/// Pay is for the 1st..15th on the 20th and for the 16th..last on the 5th. Withholding, both FICA halves, FUTA, SUTA
/// and the match come from `employment` and the plan; a paystub is one line. [A3]
contract dana-pay : employment
  employee dana                               // dana is also an owner: two relators between the same two agents, no conflict
  employer lantern-row                        // the plan is inferred: lantern-row sponsors exactly one 401k-plan
  2_750.00 USD semi-monthly in arrears paid 5, 20     // ✗ sb-c06 [A6] a pay period (16..last) and its pay date (the 5th) are two calendars, and the date moves off weekends
  deferral 10%
contract marisol-pay : employment
  employee marisol
  employer lantern-row
  2_300.00 USD semi-monthly in arrears paid 5, 20
  deferral 6%
contract kenji-pay : employment
  employee kenji
  employer lantern-row
  1_100.00 USD semi-monthly in arrears paid 5, 20
contract jonah-pay : employment
  employee jonah
  employer lantern-row
  20.50 USD/HR semi-monthly in arrears paid 5, 20     // ✎ sb-b29 [A3] a promise priced by a rate on a measure (the `worked` hours of the period), not an amount per period
  overtime 1.5 x
  deferral 3%

contract warehouse-lease : lease
  tenant lantern-row
  landlord pecan-st
  4_200.00 USD monthly on 1 from operating #rent
  deposit 4_200.00 USD                        // paid to the landlord at the start: a claim on it, back at the end

contract draws
  8_000.00 USD monthly on 25 from operating -> owners by share #distribution   // ✗ sb-c09 [A4] `owners` as an end of a leg, split by the weights; no party is invented for a category

// ── what the kinds above rely on (a sketch of us/payroll, us/s-corp and std) ─────────────────────────

kind employment : contract
  has employee  person
  has employer  org
  has plan      401k-plan optional = employer.401k-plan       // a default is evaluated the day the contract starts, then it is an ordinary step of the timeline
  has deferral  percent = 0%
  purpose wages
  also withholding(gross - deferral * gross, employee.filing) -> irs #federal-tax
  also 6.2% of gross -> irs #payroll-tax
  also 1.45% of gross -> irs #payroll-tax
  also deferral * gross -> plan.custodian #deferral
  also 6.2% of gross -> irs #payroll-tax            when employer is owner      // the employer's half: only the employer's book pays it
  also 1.45% of gross -> irs #payroll-tax           when employer is owner
  also plan.match(deferral, gross) -> plan.custodian #match  when employer is owner       // the tiers above, as a function
  also 0.6% * min(gross, max(7_000 USD - total(#wages of employee, year), empty)) -> irs #futa  when employer is owner   // ✗ sb-c02 [A5] total() cannot see the wages paid before the book began
  also 2.7% * min(gross, max(9_000 USD - total(#wages of employee, year), empty)) -> twc #suta  when employer is owner

kind s-corp : business
  has owners  person | household  some by share
  passes-through                                    // every tally the company counts is also counted for each owner, share by day  [A4]

kind stock-in-trade : commodity
  law cost-of-goods
    on gain
    derive -> basis #cost-of-goods                  // a leg out of the position the parcels left, to no party: their basis leaves the owners as spending; the proceeds keep the sale's own purpose


