// ═════ index of marks ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//   id      mark  closed by  what
//   sb-b01  ✎     [A12]    `lives us/wa` stands for nexus: a company is governed where it sells, from the day its own 12-month sales cross a threshold, not where it lives
//   sb-b03  ✎     [A9]     what selling a commodity is for is a property of the commodity's kind (`sells`), which v4 only has for issuers (`pays`)
//   sb-b07  ✎     [A1]     a tiered employer match is a typed value of the plan, not an expression repeated in every `also`
//   sb-b10  ✎     [A10]    an exchange between two of my own positions (goods in the warehouse, money into the processor): `@` has one subject position
//   sb-b12  ✎     [open]   a document that covers a half-month is one flow on one day: balances in between are wrong; order-level sync would not have this
//   sb-b14  ✎     [A10]    `<-` with `due`: a purchase whose price is owed; v5 §6.1 defines the junction for money lines only
//   sb-b19  ✎     [A9]     an inventory count whose gap is a loss of stock: `=` has `!` (unexplained) and `via` (a party, the market), not a purpose
//   sb-b21  ✎     [K5]     a late fee that repeats every 30 days: `due ... else ITEM` fires once in v4; the term algebra has `Every` inside `otherwise`
//   sb-b22  ✎     [A10]    a conversion between two of my own positions with the fee in the source currency
//   sb-b27  ✎     [A6]     the January installment belongs to the year before: an installment `for the tax year`
//   sb-b28  ✎     [A6]     a due day that falls on a weekend or holiday rolls to the next business day (taxes) or back to the day before (pay)
//   sb-b29  ✎     [A3]     a promise priced by a rate on a measure (hours worked in the pay period) rather than an amount per period
//   sb-c02  ✗     [A5]     year-to-date tallies at the start of a book: FUTA/SUTA/Social Security wage bases, 401(k) deferrals, K-1 income to date
//   sb-c04  ✗     [A7]     a revolving credit line: draws and repayments at will, interest on the daily balance, a floating rate (ACTUS UMP, IPAC)
//   sb-c05  ✗     [A8]     an interest-only note with the principal due at the end (ACTUS PAM): v5's `loan` is the annuity
//   sb-c06  ✗     [A6]     a pay period and its pay date are two calendars (16th..last paid on the 5th), and the date moves off weekends and holidays
//   sb-c09  ✗     [A4]     owners as one end of a leg split by share; a norm over per-owner tallies (distributions must be pro rata)
//   sb-c10  ✗     [A9]     selling merchandise realizes revenue and a cost, never a capital gain: the cost leg comes from the commodity's kind
//   sb-c11  ✗     [open]   a sales-tax rate is by the order's ship-to place; only the order-level document knows it, so the book types the totals it was given
//   sb-c13  ✗     [A9]     landed cost: a later freight bill joins the parcels of the purchase it belongs to, pro rata to cost
//   sb-c15  ✗     [A9]     a return goes back to stock at the cost it left with; a damaged one is not stock
//   sb-c17  ✗     [A8]     annual subscriptions sold for cash: a promise of goods bought up front; revenue as each box goes out (no `received`, no in-kind amortization)
//   sb-c20  ✗     [A6]     accrued wages at month end: the pay occurrence must cover its pay period so the expense lands in the period earned
//   sb-c24  ✗     [A4]     K-1: the company's tallies reach each owner by share and day; equity and stock basis as views, not accounts
//   sb-c25  ✗     [open]   two bases at once: books accrual, tax cash; §179 expensing for tax, five-year straight line for the books
//   sb-c26  ✗     [open]   W-2, W-3, 940, 941, 1099-NEC and K-1 as documents out: Axiom reports lines, `filed` records a return but nothing writes one
//   sb-s30  ⇄     [sync]   the store's order export, one document per half-month with units by SKU, taxes by state, fees and discounts; it outranks the Stripe lines
//   sb-s31  ⇄     [sync]   the time clock's hours per pay period, regular and overtime, as `worked` statements
//   sb-s32  ⇄     [sync]   utility, freight and postage statements as `owes` statements with their codes
//   sb-s34  ⇄     [sync]   the distributor's invoice as a priced exchange with its due day
//   sb-s35  ⇄     [sync]   the time sheet that the consulting invoice bills
//   sb-u08  ?     [A12]    a vendor that is also a client: party kinds are roles, but a thing has one kind, so the purpose rule by kind gives the wrong answer for money from it
//   sb-u16  ?     [open]   is the sales tax on a lost chargeback recoverable? A rule of the state: a param of `us/wa`, or nothing
//   sb-u18  ?     [A8]     prepaid insurance and unearned revenue have no home in `balance`: `for PERIOD` is a recognition map, not a position
//   sb-u23  ?     [open]   §988(e) exempts a personal currency gain of 200 USD or less; a business has no such exemption: content of `us/s-corp`
